In quillmark, a nil Theme field on a Doc indicates the default theme; metric labels should use 'default' in this case.
The `Doc` struct has a `Theme *theme.Theme` field where `nil` means the default theme. When labeling metrics with the theme name, dereferencing `d.Theme.Name` causes a nil pointer panic if no theme is specified. The fix is to use a helper function that returns "default" when `d.Theme == nil`, otherwise returning `d.Theme.Name`.

```go
func themeLabel(d *Doc) string {
    if d.Theme == nil {
        return "default"
    }
    return d.Theme.Name
}
```
